	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41811</id><title>Businesses Impact Nature on Which They Depend — IPBES Report Finds</title><updated>2025-12-04T12:47:13-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41811" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/IPBES-scaled.jpeg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/IPBES-scaled.jpeg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
PRETORIA, December 4 (IPS)  - Nature is a double-edged sword for global business. A groundbreaking report will reveal how businesses profit from exploiting natural resources while simultaneously impacting biodiversity.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41811&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Businesses Impact Nature on Which They Depend — IPBES Report Finds”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/IPBES-scaled-100x100.jpeg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41810</id><title>‘Low- and Middle-Income Countries Need Better Data, Not Just Better Tech’</title><updated>2025-12-04T08:56:48-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41810" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Johanna-Choumert-Nkolo-third-from-right-spekaing-during-a-panel-discussion-at-Global-Development-Conference-2025-in-Clermont-Ferrand-France__-Photo-by-Athar-Parvaiz_IPS.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Johanna-Choumert-Nkolo-third-from-right-spekaing-during-a-panel-discussion-at-Global-Development-Conference-2025-in-Clermont-Ferrand-France__-Photo-by-Athar-Parvaiz_IPS.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
CLERMONT-FERRAND, France, December 4 (IPS)  - During the Global Development Conference 2025, development experts and researchers kept warning that low- and middle-income countries (LMICs) were being pushed into a wave of digital transformation without the basic statistical systems, institutional capacity, and local context needed to ensure that AI and digital tools truly benefited the poor.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41810&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “‘Low- and Middle-Income Countries Need Better Data, Not Just Better Tech’”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Johanna-Choumert-Nkolo-third-from-right-spekaing-during-a-panel-discussion-at-Global-Development-Conference-2025-in-Clermont-Ferrand-France__-Photo-by-Athar-Parvaiz_IPS-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41809</id><title>For 78 Years, the Palestinians have Been Denied their Inalienable Rights &amp; their Right to Self-Determination</title><updated>2025-12-04T07:57:11-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41809" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/For-78-Years_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/For-78-Years_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, December 4 (IPS)  - For seventy-eight years, the question of Palestine has been on the agenda of this General Assembly, almost as long as the institution itself.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41809&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “For 78 Years, the Palestinians have Been Denied their Inalienable Rights &amp; their Right to Self-Determination”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/For-78-Years_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41808</id><title>Fresh Lens For Nuanced Multifaceted Climate Solutions Needed</title><updated>2025-12-04T07:17:39-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41808" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Drone-view-from-Combu-Island-with-the-city-of-Belem-where-COP30-took-place-in-the-background.-Credit-Alex-FerroCOP30.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Drone-view-from-Combu-Island-with-the-city-of-Belem-where-COP30-took-place-in-the-background.-Credit-Alex-FerroCOP30.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
SRINAGAR, December 4 (IPS)  - “I see more philanthropic support aligning with systems thinking, linking climate stability, biodiversity protection, Indigenous leadership, and community resilience,” says Michael Northrop, Program Director at the Rockefeller Brothers Fund.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41808&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Fresh Lens For Nuanced Multifaceted Climate Solutions Needed”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Drone-view-from-Combu-Island-with-the-city-of-Belem-where-COP30-took-place-in-the-background.-Credit-Alex-FerroCOP30-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41819</id><title>UN and partners back new measures to help millions move from vulnerability to opportunity</title><updated>2025-12-04T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41819" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/21-07-2025-UNICEF-Nepal.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/21-07-2025-UNICEF-Nepal.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A major UN meeting in Doha wrapped up on Thursday with a renewed drive to help the world’s poorest countries move towards long-term stability and prosperity, as senior officials urged stronger global partnerships to ensure that development gains are not lost once States exit the Least Developed Country (LDC) category.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41819&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN and partners back new measures to help millions move from vulnerability to opportunity”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/21-07-2025-UNICEF-Nepal.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41818</id><title>UN support helps Gaza mothers give birth amid collapsing health system</title><updated>2025-12-04T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41818" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-07-2025-UNFPA-Gaza-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-07-2025-UNFPA-Gaza-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every week in Gaza, at least 15 women give birth outside any health facility, often without a trained midwife, pain relief or basic medical supplies. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41818&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN support helps Gaza mothers give birth amid collapsing health system”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-07-2025-UNFPA-Gaza-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41817</id><title>Deadly storms sweep South and Southeast Asia, leaving over 1,600 dead</title><updated>2025-12-04T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41817" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/04-12-2025-UNICEF-Sri_Lanka-Landslide.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/04-12-2025-UNICEF-Sri_Lanka-Landslide.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;From Sri Lanka’s central highlands to Indonesia’s flood-swollen river basins, a wave of climate-fuelled cyclones and monsoon rains has unleashed one of the deadliest weather patterns south and southeast Asia has seen in years, killing more than 1,600 people, displacing hundreds of thousands and affecting millions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41817&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Deadly storms sweep South and Southeast Asia, leaving over 1,600 dead”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/04-12-2025-UNICEF-Sri_Lanka-Landslide.jpeg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41816</id><title>African football legends join forces to give a red card to polio</title><updated>2025-12-04T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41816" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/27-08-2024-UNICEF_DRC_Children_Vaccine_Polio.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/27-08-2024-UNICEF_DRC_Children_Vaccine_Polio.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Six African football legends are urging the continent to unite and step up efforts to vaccinate every child against the life-threatening polio virus.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41816&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “African football legends join forces to give a red card to polio”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/27-08-2024-UNICEF_DRC_Children_Vaccine_Polio.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41815</id><title>Amid Sudan’s unimaginable crisis, its people endure with hope</title><updated>2025-12-04T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41815" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/04-12-2025-OHCHR-Li3.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/04-12-2025-OHCHR-Li3.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As the world prepares to mark Human Rights Day on 10 December, the UN is warning that war-torn Sudan is in the midst of arguably the gravest human rights crisis of our time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41815&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Amid Sudan’s unimaginable crisis, its people endure with hope”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/04-12-2025-OHCHR-Li3.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41814</id><title>Sudan: Kordofan cannot become ‘another El Fasher,’ Türk warns</title><updated>2025-12-04T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41814" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/12-11-2025-UNICEF-Sudan-14.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/12-11-2025-UNICEF-Sudan-14.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UN human rights chief Volker Türk on Thursday warned that Sudan risks “another El Fasher” as fierce fighting spreads across the Kordofan region, raising fears of a fresh wave of atrocities. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/04/41814&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Sudan: Kordofan cannot become ‘another El Fasher,’ Türk warns”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/12-11-2025-UNICEF-Sudan-14.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry></feed><!-- 0.0018s -->